brepjs-mesh2solid
Copyright 2026 Andy Aragon

This package contains a WebAssembly mesh-processing engine compiled from
original Rust source in engine/, distributed under the Apache License 2.0
(see LICENSE).

Algorithms are clean-room implementations of published methods:

- Mesh decimation: Garland & Heckbert, "Surface Simplification Using Quadric
  Error Metrics", SIGGRAPH 1997.
- Polygon triangulation: ear clipping with hole bridging (Eberly, "Triangulation
  by Ear Clipping", Geometric Tools, 2002).
- Closest point on triangle: Ericson, "Real-Time Collision Detection", 2005,
  section 5.1.5.

The WebAssembly binary also contains these Rust crates, each used under the
license named (for dual- or multi-licensed crates, the option elected here):

- wasm-bindgen, wasm-bindgen-shared, cfg-if, once_cell (MIT OR Apache-2.0):
  Apache-2.0
- miniz_oxide (MIT OR Zlib OR Apache-2.0): Apache-2.0
- adler2 (0BSD OR MIT OR Apache-2.0): Apache-2.0
- memchr (Unlicense OR MIT): Unlicense
